# Google Calendar (read-only overlay on the Calendar view)
#
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or pick) a project.
# 2. Enable the "Google Calendar API" under APIs & Services > Library.
# 3. Configure the OAuth consent screen (External, testing is fine while
#    this is just you/your phone) and add the `.../auth/calendar.readonly`
#    scope.
# 4. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID under APIs & Services > Credentials,
#    type "Web application". Add every origin you'll actually load this app
#    from to "Authorized JavaScript origins" (e.g. http://localhost:5173,
#    plus wherever you test from on your phone).
# 5. Copy this file to .env.local and paste the Client ID below. This value
#    is public (it's sent to the browser), not a secret — do not put the
#    Client Secret here, it isn't used by this app at all.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
